From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Date: Sun, 23 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] devfreq: rockchip: add RK3568 DMC devfreq driver

Add a DMC (Dynamic Memory Controller) devfreq driver for RK3566/RK3568.

DDR frequency scaling uses the BSP V2 SIP protocol with MCU-based DCF:
 1. Kernel requests shared memory via SIP_SHARE_MEM (0x82000009)
 2. Kernel writes target Hz to the shared page
 3. SET_RATE SIP call returns -6 ("started, wait for MCU completion")
 4. Kernel starts the MCU via MCU_START SIP sub-command
 5. MCU performs the HWFFC and fires a completion IRQ (GIC_SPI 10)
 6. IRQ handler calls POST_SET_RATE for cleanup

This protocol follows the Rockchip BSP DMC driver behaviour (ATF
version 0x102 or newer).

Signed-off-by: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
---
 drivers/devfreq/Kconfig      |  12 +
 drivers/devfreq/Makefile     |   1 +
 drivers/devfreq/rk3568_dmc.c | 639 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 653 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/devfreq/rk3568_dmc.c

